			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Reduce high-frequency log noise in default mode\n\nMove per-call firehose logs (vfs, grpc, storage, ipc operations) to verbose variants that are muted in `short` mode:\n\n1. **DevLog infrastructure** (`DevLog.rs`):\n   - Add `SHORT_MODE_MUTED_TAGS` constant listing tags silenced by `short` mode\n   - Update `IsEnabled()` to respect muted list while preserving explicit tag overrides\n\n2. **gRPC layer** (`MountainVinegRPCService.rs`):\n   - Move per-request banners to `grpc-verbose`: receive, dispatch, params, completion\n   - Move latency timestamps to `rpc-latency` for profiling\n   - Extend 404 downgrade to both `FileSystem.ReadFile` and `FileSystem.Stat`\n   - Move notification receive banners to `grpc-verbose`\n\n3. **VFS operations** (all FileSystem handlers):\n   - Change `vfs` → `vfs-verbose` for stat/read/write/mkdir/delete/copy/move operations\n   - Per-path stat fires thousands of times during workbench boot\n\n4. **Storage operations** (`StorageProvider.rs`, `SecretProvider.rs`):\n   - Change `storage` → `storage-verbose` for updateItems, getAllStorage, setAllStorage\n   - Short-form storage logs also use `storage-verbose` for consistency\n\n5. **IPC routing** (`WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`):\n   - Expand high-frequency skip list to include file:stat, file:readFile, file:readdir, file:writeFile, storage:getItems, storage:updateItems, configuration:lookup, configuration:inspect, themes:getColorTheme\n   - These fire thousands of times per session and add no signal beyond the IPC summary line\n\n6. **NLS scanning** (`Scanner.rs`):\n   - Change `extensions` → `nls` for NLS placeholder resolution and bundle loading\n\n7. **Tree latency** (`TreeView.rs`, `DispatchSideCarRequest.rs`):\n   - Change `grpc` → `tree-latency` / `grpc-verbose` for dispatch timing\n\nThis reduces default log volume from ~14k+ lines per session to ~500, while preserving full verbosity via `LAND_DEV_LOG=all` or explicit tag matching. The failure paths for each subsystem still log at the default level, so errors remain visible.",
			"SHA": "9aa00458dcaa47d38fe44223376a186373386db0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T16:45:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Expand trusted paths and add exec-bit magic-number detection\n\nThree complementary improvements for extension runtime reliability:\n\n1. **Extended trusted paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`):\n   - Add `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/tmp` for language servers (ruby-lsp, pyright, etc.)\n   - Add third-party tool state: `~/.gitkraken`, `~/.gk`, `~/.copilot`, `~/.config/git`\n   - Add read-only POSIX OS files (`/etc/os-release`, `/proc/*`, etc.)\n\n2. **Magic-number executable detection** (`VsixInstaller.rs`):\n   - Enhance extraction to probe file headers for ELF, Mach-O fat/thin, and shebang\n   - Detect bin paths (`bin/`, `server/`, `tools/`, `omnisharp`, `adapter`, `native`)\n   - Promote 0o644 → 0o755 for detected executables, fixing EACCES on spawn\n   - Add `HealExecutableBits()` to retroactively fix pre-existing installs\n\n3. **Boot-time exec-bit heal** (`Scanner.rs`):\n   - Walk user extensions (`~/.land/extensions/`) at scan time\n   - Apply same heuristic to recover extensions installed before the fix\n\n4. **Benign ENOENT** (`DevLog.rs`):\n   - Add vim registers, globalStorage probing, chat editing sessions\n\nThese changes unblock extension binaries (rust-analyzer, GitLens, Copilot) that were failing with EACCES due to missing exec bits.",
			"SHA": "713fc89729f6f995808d00db9ca625cdfc93f906"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:07:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add trusted system paths bypass and idempotent VSIX installs\n\nImplement two related extension-management improvements:\n\n1. **Trusted system paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`): Add `IsTrustedSystemPath` that defines directories Land owns (`.land/`, Application Support, bundled extension roots, TMPDIR) which bypass the workspace-folder sandbox check. Without this, the extension scanner's read of `~/.land/extensions` was rejected as \"outside workspace\" - user-installed VSIXes never reached the Extensions sidebar.\n\n2. **Idempotent VSIX reinstalls** (`VsixInstaller.rs`): Remove `AlreadyInstalled` error and instead treat re-installs as no-op when the target already exists with a readable manifest. Matches VS Code's semantics and prevents the renderer crash where `ExtensionsWorkbenchService` dereferences a null result. Corrupt/partial installs are wiped and re-extracted.\n\nBoth changes unblock the extension loading pipeline.",
			"SHA": "e49563563641f0491ec4cb23c2ea1809d455feea"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T14:49:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Add payload preview to notif-drop logging and register benign ENOENT paths\n\nTwo logging improvements for Mountain's developer diagnostics:\n\n1. **Notif-drop payload preview**: When a notification falls through to the Cocoon event handler, include a truncated payload preview (160 bytes max) in the dev log. This helps diagnose which new upstream notifications are reaching the catch-all without needing a second debug run.\n\n2. **Benign ENOENT paths**: Register additional file paths that commonly return ENOENT but aren't errors:\n   - MCP config files (.vscode/mcp.json, .mcp.json)\n   - User snippets and keybindings (/User/snippets, /User/keybindings.json)\n   - AI-generated workspace storage (aiGeneratedWorkspaces.json)\n   - Git config for non-repo folders (/.git/config)\n\nThese paths reduce noise in dev logs while preserving signal for genuine file-access issues.",
			"SHA": "f1de83d594ad1a3f7c893f0ecbf92581f8029abb"
